{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017x2PSUH5iN4U3jmBNCGazi","type":"tool_result","content":"# Architecture Decision Records\n\nDecisions that are hard to reverse, surprising without context, and the\nresult of a real trade-off. See `docs/agents/domain.md` for how agents\nconsume these and `CONTEXT.md` for the project glossary.\n\n| # | Decision | Date |\n|---|----------|------|\n| [ADR-001](ADR-001-alien-signals-for-reactivity.md) | alien-signals as the reactivity primitive | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-002](ADR-002-no-shadow-dom.md) | No Shadow DOM | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-003](ADR-003-standard-schema-for-prop-validation.md) | Standard Schema for prop validation | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-004](ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md) | Client bundle size outranks API ergonomics | 2026-07-25 |\n| [ADR-005](ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md) | Single-file components with build-time stripping of render code | 2026-09-23 |\n| [ADR-006][adr-006] | Authored HTML scaffold served by Hono | 2026-09-25 |\n| [ADR-007][adr-007] | Client templater: signal props, reactive regions, mount | 2026-10-04 |\n| [ADR-008][adr-008] | Serialized server state and unidirectional hydration | 2026-10-04 |\n\n[adr-006]: ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\n[adr-007]: ADR-007-client-templater.md\n[adr-008]: ADR-008-serialized-server-state.md\n# ADR-005: Single-file components with build-time stripping of render code\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-23\n\n## Context\n\nA component is a client-only module. It exposes its tag name and ref\nnames as statics so a server template can reference them, but the markup\nitself lives in a separate server file (for example `example/ssr.ts`).\nOne component is split across two files, and the server file drifts from\nthe behaviour it describes. There is also no way to compose components\ninto a page as strings with escaping and nested expansion.\n\nMoving the markup into the component would ship it to every browser, and\nADR-004 forbids that. Alternatives considered:\n\n- Keep the separate server file. Rejected: drift is the problem.\n- Markup in the component, always shipped. Rejected under ADR-004.\n- A `<template>` element or declarative shadow DOM. Rejected: the\n  template still has to be authored on the server, and ADR-002 rules out\n  shadow roots.\n- Usage analysis that keeps render code automatically for classes used in\n  an `html` template. Deferred; too much machinery for the first cut.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe builder gains a `.render(fn, { client? })` link before `.setup`. The\nrender function receives plain props, the ref name map, the tag, and\ncaller-supplied children and attrs, and returns the host's inner HTML.\nAfter `setup`, the element class exposes statics `render` and `props`\nbeside `TAG` and `refs`. The attribute serializer and host-tag wrapper\nlive in the core entry, because the static `render` must call them and a\nclass member cannot be tree-shaken.\n\nAn `html` tagged template in a separate subpath, `microtags/html`,\ncomposes pages and expands components recursively. It is built on `htm`,\nwhich stays out of the core entry. Interpolated strings are escaped;\nrender output and `raw` strings are trusted.\n\nA Node-only transform in `microtags/build` strips `.render(...)` from the\nclient code. The rule is syntactic: a `.render` link in a call chain\nrooted at the `define` binding imported from `microtags`, with aliases\ntracked. Removed spans become newlines so line numbers survive. An\noptional cascade then removes imports and top-level declarations that only\nthe stripped code used. A component opts out with `{ client: true }` in\nsource or a `keep` list at build time. The parser is the `typescript`\npackage as an optional peer dependency. The transform ships as esbuild and\nVite plugins and as a `microbuild` CLI.\n\nImplementation is tracked under `.scratch/ssr-render-and-microbuild/`.\n\n## Consequences\n\nMarkup and behaviour have one source of truth, and a browser bundle\ncontains hydration code only. Other server templaters, such as Hono, can\ncall the static `render` directly.\n\nThe type declares `render` as always present while it is `undefined` at\nruntime after stripping; this gap is accepted and documented. The build\nstep is opt-in, so import-map consumers ship render code, consistent with\nADR-004. `client: true` is only recognised in an object literal, and the\nnon-chained form `const b = define('x'); b.render(fn)` is unsupported.\nThe transform adds `typescript` as a peer for anyone who uses it. The\ncore size budget stays at 3.5 kB, and the delta from the serializer is\nmeasured and reported.\n\n## Note (2026-10-04)\n\n[ADR-007](./ADR-007-client-templater.md) changes the templater's return\ntype: `html`, `h`, and `raw` return opaque markup instead of a string,\nand callers that need HTML convert with `String(m)`. The render function\nmay return markup. A component that the browser creates (from `mount` or\na reactive region) must be kept, with `client: true` or the build-time\nkeep list; creating a stripped component throws. This ADR is not\nsuperseded.\n      26 src/attributes.ts\n     536 src/build.ts\n     485 src/builders.ts\n     180 src/cli.ts\n      93 src/context.ts\n      49 src/esbuild.ts\n     247 src/factory.ts\n     523 src/htm.browser.ts\n     190 src/htm.ts\n      12 src/index.ts\n      32 src/reactivity.ts\n      89 src/render.ts\n     119 src/setup-context.ts\n     219 src/types.ts\n      83 src/util.ts\n      53 src/vite.ts\n    2936 total\n// .size-limit.js\nexport default [\n    {\n        name: 'microtags',\n        path: 'dist/index.min.js',\n        limit: '4.2 kB',\n    },\n    {\n        name: 'microtags/htm',\n        path: 'dist/htm.min.js',\n        limit: '5 kB',\n    },\n    {\n        name: 'microtags/htm (browser)',\n        path: 'dist/htm.browser.min.js',\n        limit: '4.6 kB',\n    },\n]\n{\n  \"name\": \"microtags\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.14\",\n  \"description\": \"Web component helper\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/index.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/index.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./min\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/index.min.js\"\n    },\n    \"./render\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/render.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/render.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/render.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./context\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/context.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/context.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/context.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./util\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/util.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/util.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/util.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./build\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/build.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/build.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/build.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./esbuild\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/esbuild.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/esbuild.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/esbuild.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./vite\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/vite.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/vite.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/vite.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./htm\": {\n      \"browser\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/htm.browser.d.ts\",\n        \"import\": \"./dist/htm.browser.js\"\n      },\n      \"types\": \"./dist/htm.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/htm.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/htm.cjs\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"microbuild\": \"./dist/cli.cjs\"\n  },\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n.scratch/:\nhydration-dx-fixes/\nmillitags-lessons/\nunidirectional-hydration/\n\n.scratch/unidirectional-hydration/:\nissues/\nlogs/\nprogress.md\nreview-2026-10-13-hydration-dx.md\nspec.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa7c6907-4b1d-4b07-bcee-1f7f5e6cee2e","uuid":"452eebdf-b4ef-4dba-adfc-b9e04552e06a","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:05:21.850Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Architecture Decision Records\n\nDecisions that are hard to reverse, surprising without context, and the\nresult of a real trade-off. See `docs/agents/domain.md` for how agents\nconsume these and `CONTEXT.md` for the project glossary.\n\n| # | Decision | Date |\n|---|----------|------|\n| [ADR-001](ADR-001-alien-signals-for-reactivity.md) | alien-signals as the reactivity primitive | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-002](ADR-002-no-shadow-dom.md) | No Shadow DOM | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-003](ADR-003-standard-schema-for-prop-validation.md) | Standard Schema for prop validation | 2026-06-28 |\n| [ADR-004](ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md) | Client bundle size outranks API ergonomics | 2026-07-25 |\n| [ADR-005](ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md) | Single-file components with build-time stripping of render code | 2026-09-23 |\n| [ADR-006][adr-006] | Authored HTML scaffold served by Hono | 2026-09-25 |\n| [ADR-007][adr-007] | Client templater: signal props, reactive regions, mount | 2026-10-04 |\n| [ADR-008][adr-008] | Serialized server state and unidirectional hydration | 2026-10-04 |\n\n[adr-006]: ADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\n[adr-007]: ADR-007-client-templater.md\n[adr-008]: ADR-008-serialized-server-state.md\n# ADR-005: Single-file components with build-time stripping of render code\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-23\n\n## Context\n\nA component is a client-only module. It exposes its tag name and ref\nnames as statics so a server template can reference them, but the markup\nitself lives in a separate server file (for example `example/ssr.ts`).\nOne component is split across two files, and the server file drifts from\nthe behaviour it describes. There is also no way to compose components\ninto a page as strings with escaping and nested expansion.\n\nMoving the markup into the component would ship it to every browser, and\nADR-004 forbids that. Alternatives considered:\n\n- Keep the separate server file. Rejected: drift is the problem.\n- Markup in the component, always shipped. Rejected under ADR-004.\n- A `<template>` element or declarative shadow DOM. Rejected: the\n  template still has to be authored on the server, and ADR-002 rules out\n  shadow roots.\n- Usage analysis that keeps render code automatically for classes used in\n  an `html` template. Deferred; too much machinery for the first cut.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe builder gains a `.render(fn, { client? })` link before `.setup`. The\nrender function receives plain props, the ref name map, the tag, and\ncaller-supplied children and attrs, and returns the host's inner HTML.\nAfter `setup`, the element class exposes statics `render` and `props`\nbeside `TAG` and `refs`. The attribute serializer and host-tag wrapper\nlive in the core entry, because the static `render` must call them and a\nclass member cannot be tree-shaken.\n\nAn `html` tagged template in a separate subpath, `microtags/html`,\ncomposes pages and expands components recursively. It is built on `htm`,\nwhich stays out of the core entry. Interpolated strings are escaped;\nrender output and `raw` strings are trusted.\n\nA Node-only transform in `microtags/build` strips `.render(...)` from the\nclient code. The rule is syntactic: a `.render` link in a call chain\nrooted at the `define` binding imported from `microtags`, with aliases\ntracked. Removed spans become newlines so line numbers survive. An\noptional cascade then removes imports and top-level declarations that only\nthe stripped code used. A component opts out with `{ client: true }` in\nsource or a `keep` list at build time. The parser is the `typescript`\npackage as an optional peer dependency. The transform ships as esbuild and\nVite plugins and as a `microbuild` CLI.\n\nImplementation is tracked under `.scratch/ssr-render-and-microbuild/`.\n\n## Consequences\n\nMarkup and behaviour have one source of truth, and a browser bundle\ncontains hydration code only. Other server templaters, such as Hono, can\ncall the static `render` directly.\n\nThe type declares `render` as always present while it is `undefined` at\nruntime after stripping; this gap is accepted and documented. The build\nstep is opt-in, so import-map consumers ship render code, consistent with\nADR-004. `client: true` is only recognised in an object literal, and the\nnon-chained form `const b = define('x'); b.render(fn)` is unsupported.\nThe transform adds `typescript` as a peer for anyone who uses it. The\ncore size budget stays at 3.5 kB, and the delta from the serializer is\nmeasured and reported.\n\n## Note (2026-10-04)\n\n[ADR-007](./ADR-007-client-templater.md) changes the templater's return\ntype: `html`, `h`, and `raw` return opaque markup instead of a string,\nand callers that need HTML convert with `String(m)`. The render function\nmay return markup. A component that the browser creates (from `mount` or\na reactive region) must be kept, with `client: true` or the build-time\nkeep list; creating a stripped component throws. This ADR is not\nsuperseded.\n      26 src/attributes.ts\n     536 src/build.ts\n     485 src/builders.ts\n     180 src/cli.ts\n      93 src/context.ts\n      49 src/esbuild.ts\n     247 src/factory.ts\n     523 src/htm.browser.ts\n     190 src/htm.ts\n      12 src/index.ts\n      32 src/reactivity.ts\n      89 src/render.ts\n     119 src/setup-context.ts\n     219 src/types.ts\n      83 src/util.ts\n      53 src/vite.ts\n    2936 total\n// .size-limit.js\nexport default [\n    {\n        name: 'microtags',\n        path: 'dist/index.min.js',\n        limit: '4.2 kB',\n    },\n    {\n        name: 'microtags/htm',\n        path: 'dist/htm.min.js',\n        limit: '5 kB',\n    },\n    {\n        name: 'microtags/htm (browser)',\n        path: 'dist/htm.browser.min.js',\n        limit: '4.6 kB',\n    },\n]\n{\n  \"name\": \"microtags\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.14\",\n  \"description\": \"Web component helper\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/index.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/index.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./min\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/index.min.js\"\n    },\n    \"./render\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/render.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/render.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/render.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./context\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/context.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/context.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/context.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./util\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/util.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/util.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/util.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./build\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/build.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/build.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/build.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./esbuild\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/esbuild.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/esbuild.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/esbuild.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./vite\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/vite.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/vite.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/vite.cjs\"\n    },\n    \"./htm\": {\n      \"browser\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/htm.browser.d.ts\",\n        \"import\": \"./dist/htm.browser.js\"\n      },\n      \"types\": \"./dist/htm.d.ts\",\n      \"import\": \"./dist/htm.js\",\n      \"require\": \"./dist/htm.cjs\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"microbuild\": \"./dist/cli.cjs\"\n  },\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n.scratch/:\nhydration-dx-fixes/\nmillitags-lessons/\nunidirectional-hydration/\n\n.scratch/unidirectional-hydration/:\nissues/\nlogs/\nprogress.md\nreview-2026-10-13-hydration-dx.md\nspec.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017x2PSUH5iN4U3jmBNCGazi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
