{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LfJP4YqeoNrezzW8Dr8j6F","type":"tool_result","content":"67:Measured on the patched copy with Vite 8.3.4. The stripping-off variant\n68-uses a scratch config with the `microtags()` plugin set to `null`.\n69-\n70-| Bundle | Minified | gzip | Unminified |\n71-|---|---|---|---|\n72-| Client, stripping on (as shipped) | 23,113 B | 8.66 kB | 45.08 kB |\n73-| Client, stripping off | 23.88 kB | 8.80 kB | 45.91 kB |\n74-| Server `app.js` | not minified | 8,236 B | 26,087 B |\n75-| Server `listen.js` | not minified | n/a | 896 B |\n76-\n77-Stripping saves 0.77 kB minified (3.2%) and about 0.14 kB gzip (1.6%).\n78-The unminified diff shows only Counter's render body and `raw()` were\n79-removed.\n80-\n81-Server `app.js` leaves `hono`, `alien-signals` and `htm` as external\n82-imports, so comparing the 23 kB client to the 26 kB server is not like\n83-for like. The strip on/off comparison is the meaningful one.\n84-\n85-Largest pieces of the stripped client (unminified bytes per module):\n86-\n87-- `src/htm.browser.ts` 10,921\n88-- alien-signals 9,946\n89-- `src/builders.ts` 5,597\n90-- `src/factory.ts` 4,198\n91-- `htm` 1,794\n92-- all pages together, about 3,900\n93-\n94-## Findings\n95-\n96-Ordered most severe first. Each lists the goal it threatens.\n97-\n--\n263:### 8. Important (goal 5). Stripping barely shrinks the client\n264-\n265-The stripped client still contains `_renderHost`, `_serializerFor`,\n266-`_sJson`, `_escAttr` and the `staticRender` wrapper from\n267-`src/builders.ts`, plus `_str` and `_compArgs` from `htm.browser.ts`.\n268-These are built inside `define()` and `Markup.toString`, so stripping a\n269-user's `.render` can never remove them.\n270-\n271-Core grew from 3.48 kB to 4.17 kB brotli (+20%), and the size limit was\n272-raised from 3.5 kB to 4.2 kB. The browser templater is at 4.56 kB against\n273-a 4.6 kB limit. Net effect in this example: 23.88 kB to 23.11 kB.\n274-\n275-Fix: move static-render construction out of `define()`. For example,\n276-have `.render()` attach the serializer lazily from a separate module, so\n277-stripping `.render` also drops `_renderHost` and the serializers.\n278:Measure again with all renders stripped.\n279-\n280-### 9. Minor (goal 3). Mismatch recovery cascades, and the warning is not dev-only\n281-\n282-On a tag mismatch, `_adopt` advances one DOM node (line 486), so one\n283-extra server node misaligns every later sibling.\n284-\n285-Probe: server `<h1><p><button>`, client `<p><button>`. Warnings:\n286-`expected <p>, found <h1>` then `expected <button>, found <p>`, and the\n287-button is left unbound.\n288-\n289-`console.warn` at lines 466 and 482 is unconditional.\n290-\n291-Fix: on a mismatch, look ahead for a matching tag before giving up. Gate\n292-the warning behind a dev flag, or document that it always warns.\n293-\n294-### 10. Minor (goal 4). Badge replaces its text node on every hydration\n295-\n296-`components/badge.ts:19`:\n297-\n298-```ts\n299-ctx.refs.text.textContent = ctx.props.label()\n300-```\n301-\n302-Production probe on `/list`: `add text(\"alpha\") in <span>` / `remove\n303-text(\"alpha\") from <span>` for each badge. `mount` itself creates no\n304-element nodes on any route; the churn comes from the example's setup\n305-pattern.\n306-\n307-Fix: write only when the value changes (`if (el.textContent !== v)`),\n308-and document the pattern.\n--\n345:handling (`factory.ts:118-122`). A setup that calls a method on a nested\n346-host ref would break in the stripped build only.\n347-\n348-Fix: document this, have `client/index.ts` import leaf components first,\n349-or keep side-effect imports when cascading.\n350-\n351-### 14. Minor (DX). The binding API needs type casts and leaves stale attributes\n352-\n353-`components/counter.ts:47`:\n354-\n355-```ts\n356-ctx.refs.current.label = label as unknown as string\n357-```\n358-\n359-After binding, host attributes (for example `count=\"12\"`) stop updating.\n360-\n361-Fix: a typed `bind(host, 'label', sig)` helper, or a `MicrotagHost`\n362-setter type that accepts `Signal<T>`.\n363-\n364-### 15. Minor (DX). Smaller issues\n365-\n366-- No lockfile is committed, so `npm ci` is impossible and versions float\n367-  (Vite 8.3.4 resolved against `^8.0.5`).\n368-- `key` is emitted as a real DOM attribute (`<li key=\"alpha\">`).\n369-- `/index.html` gets no `aria-current`, because route `/index.html` is\n370-  not equal to `/`.\n371-\n372-## Docs that contradict the code\n373-\n374-1. `AGENTS.md` and `example-hydration/README.md:36-37` say the config\n375-   imports from `dist/vite.js`. It imports `../src/vite.js` (finding 1).\n--\n378:   (finding 8).\n379-3. ADR-005 line 64 says \"The core size budget stays at 3.5 kB\".\n380:   `.size-limit.js` now allows 4.2 kB, and the measured size is 4.17 kB.\n381-4. ADR-007 line 92 says \"the core entry grows only by the prop\n382-   accessors\". It also grew by the serializer, `_renderHost` and the\n383-   static render (+0.69 kB brotli).\n384-5. ADR-007 line 85 says a mismatch \"warns in development\". The warning\n385-   is unconditional, and the ADR omits that later siblings misalign\n386-   (finding 9).\n387-6. ADR-007 line 70 says adoption \"binds, and creates no nodes\". That\n388-   holds for elements, but adoption rewrites every static attribute\n389-   (finding 3).\n390-\n391-## Verdict per goal\n392-\n393-1. Events up, state down: partially met. The example follows the\n394-   pattern, but the runtime lets components write the parent's state\n395-   through bound props (finding 5).\n396-2. Same code on both sides: partially met. Server attribute\n397-   serialization differs from the browser's (finding 2), and server-only\n398-   page options drift (finding 6).\n399-3. Client adds interactivity: met in logic, broken at HEAD. All e2e and\n400-   hydration tests pass once finding 1 is fixed. There are adoption gaps\n401-   for `raw()` and for regions in a component's own render (finding 4).\n402-4. No client re-render: partially met. No element nodes are created and\n403-   `innerHTML` is unchanged on all six routes, but adoption rewrites\n404-   every attribute, Badge replaces its text nodes, drifted values\n405-   overwrite server text, and the page stays hidden until JS runs\n406-   (findings 3, 6, 7, 10).\n407-5. Client bundle smaller: technically met, marginal. 23.11 kB stripped\n408-   against 23.88 kB unstripped (-3.2% minified, -1.6% gzip). Server-render\n409:   code stays in core regardless of stripping (finding 8).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa7c6907-4b1d-4b07-bcee-1f7f5e6cee2e","uuid":"554c03a1-02e0-4f28-81db-00673e28d976","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:05:22.895Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"67:Measured on the patched copy with Vite 8.3.4. The stripping-off variant\n68-uses a scratch config with the `microtags()` plugin set to `null`.\n69-\n70-| Bundle | Minified | gzip | Unminified |\n71-|---|---|---|---|\n72-| Client, stripping on (as shipped) | 23,113 B | 8.66 kB | 45.08 kB |\n73-| Client, stripping off | 23.88 kB | 8.80 kB | 45.91 kB |\n74-| Server `app.js` | not minified | 8,236 B | 26,087 B |\n75-| Server `listen.js` | not minified | n/a | 896 B |\n76-\n77-Stripping saves 0.77 kB minified (3.2%) and about 0.14 kB gzip (1.6%).\n78-The unminified diff shows only Counter's render body and `raw()` were\n79-removed.\n80-\n81-Server `app.js` leaves `hono`, `alien-signals` and `htm` as external\n82-imports, so comparing the 23 kB client to the 26 kB server is not like\n83-for like. The strip on/off comparison is the meaningful one.\n84-\n85-Largest pieces of the stripped client (unminified bytes per module):\n86-\n87-- `src/htm.browser.ts` 10,921\n88-- alien-signals 9,946\n89-- `src/builders.ts` 5,597\n90-- `src/factory.ts` 4,198\n91-- `htm` 1,794\n92-- all pages together, about 3,900\n93-\n94-## Findings\n95-\n96-Ordered most severe first. Each lists the goal it threatens.\n97-\n--\n263:### 8. Important (goal 5). Stripping barely shrinks the client\n264-\n265-The stripped client still contains `_renderHost`, `_serializerFor`,\n266-`_sJson`, `_escAttr` and the `staticRender` wrapper from\n267-`src/builders.ts`, plus `_str` and `_compArgs` from `htm.browser.ts`.\n268-These are built inside `define()` and `Markup.toString`, so stripping a\n269-user's `.render` can never remove them.\n270-\n271-Core grew from 3.48 kB to 4.17 kB brotli (+20%), and the size limit was\n272-raised from 3.5 kB to 4.2 kB. The browser templater is at 4.56 kB against\n273-a 4.6 kB limit. Net effect in this example: 23.88 kB to 23.11 kB.\n274-\n275-Fix: move static-render construction out of `define()`. For example,\n276-have `.render()` attach the serializer lazily from a separate module, so\n277-stripping `.render` also drops `_renderHost` and the serializers.\n278:Measure again with all renders stripped.\n279-\n280-### 9. Minor (goal 3). Mismatch recovery cascades, and the warning is not dev-only\n281-\n282-On a tag mismatch, `_adopt` advances one DOM node (line 486), so one\n283-extra server node misaligns every later sibling.\n284-\n285-Probe: server `<h1><p><button>`, client `<p><button>`. Warnings:\n286-`expected <p>, found <h1>` then `expected <button>, found <p>`, and the\n287-button is left unbound.\n288-\n289-`console.warn` at lines 466 and 482 is unconditional.\n290-\n291-Fix: on a mismatch, look ahead for a matching tag before giving up. Gate\n292-the warning behind a dev flag, or document that it always warns.\n293-\n294-### 10. Minor (goal 4). Badge replaces its text node on every hydration\n295-\n296-`components/badge.ts:19`:\n297-\n298-```ts\n299-ctx.refs.text.textContent = ctx.props.label()\n300-```\n301-\n302-Production probe on `/list`: `add text(\"alpha\") in <span>` / `remove\n303-text(\"alpha\") from <span>` for each badge. `mount` itself creates no\n304-element nodes on any route; the churn comes from the example's setup\n305-pattern.\n306-\n307-Fix: write only when the value changes (`if (el.textContent !== v)`),\n308-and document the pattern.\n--\n345:handling (`factory.ts:118-122`). A setup that calls a method on a nested\n346-host ref would break in the stripped build only.\n347-\n348-Fix: document this, have `client/index.ts` import leaf components first,\n349-or keep side-effect imports when cascading.\n350-\n351-### 14. Minor (DX). The binding API needs type casts and leaves stale attributes\n352-\n353-`components/counter.ts:47`:\n354-\n355-```ts\n356-ctx.refs.current.label = label as unknown as string\n357-```\n358-\n359-After binding, host attributes (for example `count=\"12\"`) stop updating.\n360-\n361-Fix: a typed `bind(host, 'label', sig)` helper, or a `MicrotagHost`\n362-setter type that accepts `Signal<T>`.\n363-\n364-### 15. Minor (DX). Smaller issues\n365-\n366-- No lockfile is committed, so `npm ci` is impossible and versions float\n367-  (Vite 8.3.4 resolved against `^8.0.5`).\n368-- `key` is emitted as a real DOM attribute (`<li key=\"alpha\">`).\n369-- `/index.html` gets no `aria-current`, because route `/index.html` is\n370-  not equal to `/`.\n371-\n372-## Docs that contradict the code\n373-\n374-1. `AGENTS.md` and `example-hydration/README.md:36-37` say the config\n375-   imports from `dist/vite.js`. It imports `../src/vite.js` (finding 1).\n--\n378:   (finding 8).\n379-3. ADR-005 line 64 says \"The core size budget stays at 3.5 kB\".\n380:   `.size-limit.js` now allows 4.2 kB, and the measured size is 4.17 kB.\n381-4. ADR-007 line 92 says \"the core entry grows only by the prop\n382-   accessors\". It also grew by the serializer, `_renderHost` and the\n383-   static render (+0.69 kB brotli).\n384-5. ADR-007 line 85 says a mismatch \"warns in development\". The warning\n385-   is unconditional, and the ADR omits that later siblings misalign\n386-   (finding 9).\n387-6. ADR-007 line 70 says adoption \"binds, and creates no nodes\". That\n388-   holds for elements, but adoption rewrites every static attribute\n389-   (finding 3).\n390-\n391-## Verdict per goal\n392-\n393-1. Events up, state down: partially met. The example follows the\n394-   pattern, but the runtime lets components write the parent's state\n395-   through bound props (finding 5).\n396-2. Same code on both sides: partially met. Server attribute\n397-   serialization differs from the browser's (finding 2), and server-only\n398-   page options drift (finding 6).\n399-3. Client adds interactivity: met in logic, broken at HEAD. All e2e and\n400-   hydration tests pass once finding 1 is fixed. There are adoption gaps\n401-   for `raw()` and for regions in a component's own render (finding 4).\n402-4. No client re-render: partially met. No element nodes are created and\n403-   `innerHTML` is unchanged on all six routes, but adoption rewrites\n404-   every attribute, Badge replaces its text nodes, drifted values\n405-   overwrite server text, and the page stays hidden until JS runs\n406-   (findings 3, 6, 7, 10).\n407-5. Client bundle smaller: technically met, marginal. 23.11 kB stripped\n408-   against 23.88 kB unstripped (-3.2% minified, -1.6% gzip). Server-render\n409:   code stays in core regardless of stripping (finding 8).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LfJP4YqeoNrezzW8Dr8j6F","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
