{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NKMxs7j2qS8ynZW9Ps","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] ADR-009 exists, is listed in the ADR index, and names one registration mechanism with the reasons the others lost\n[x] ADR-009 records measured sizes for core, the browser templater, and an all-stripped fixture bundle for the chosen mechanism, using the review's method\n[x] ADR-009 states the breaking change for code that calls a component's `render` static without a templater\n[x] `npm run lint` passes and `src/` is unchanged\n\nADR-009 picks the global hook (option C) for registering the server render support module, and all four checklist items are done. Lint passes, `src/` is unchanged and `npm test` passes 286/286. Last time the test gate failed only because port 8123 was in use. The earlier work had been lost, so I redid it.\n\n**What I built.** The prototype is in `.scratch/hydration-dx-fixes/prototype-12/`. `measure.sh <variant>` copies the repo to a temp folder and applies one variant. It then builds the minified entries plus two test components (one with every render link stripped, one keeping its render link) and measures them with `size-limit` in brotli, as the review did. It also runs the SSR suite against the copy. The baseline reproduces the review's numbers.\n\nSizes in kB, brotli:\n\n| | Now | A: subpath | B: setter | C: global hook |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| core | 4.17 | 3.90 | 3.90 | 3.92 |\n| browser templater | 4.56 | 4.81 | 4.81 | 4.80 |\n| server templater | 1.43 | 1.70 | 1.70 | 1.71 |\n| all-stripped component | 3.81 | 3.58 | 3.58 | 3.62 |\n| kept-render component | 3.84 | 3.90 | 3.89 | 3.91 |\n\nFor all three variants, the stripped component's bundle no longer contains the support module or the escape table. The SSR suite passes 79/79 unchanged in each, so the server HTML is byte-for-byte the same.\n\n**Why C.** The sizes are within 0.04 kB of each other, so packaging decided it. A and B store the registration in a variable inside core, which only works if core and the templater share one copy of that module. The CJS build and the `.min.js` builds bundle each entry on its own, so they don't share it. I checked: with A, `require('microtags')` plus `require('microtags/htm')` throws on the first render, and so does loading core and the templater from two copies of the source. C renders in both cases.\n\n**Found while prototyping.** If the support module checks which coercer a prop uses by comparing functions, a boolean prop from another copy comes out as `open=\"true\"`. So core now records each prop's kind (`boolean`, `json` and so on) itself.\n\n**Effects for the next tickets:**\n- The ADR states the breaking change: code that calls `El.render` directly, without a templater, must import `microtags/render-support` once.\n- It also says the hydration example still ships the support module, because it keeps Badge and Notice.\n- The browser templater will go over its 4.6 kB limit and needs raising under the spec's rule.\n- The suggested core budget is 3.95 kB; ticket 13 sets the final number.\n- If the record core passes to the support module changes shape, the hook's key has to change too.\n- ADR-005 itself is not edited yet; ticket 13 adds its note.\n\nI also added a short note to `AGENTS.md`: `npm run lint` covers `.scratch/**/*.ts`, and it explains how to measure a core change in a temp copy. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md` (not committed)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":624,"cache_read_input_tokens":104456,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":624},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa7c6907-4b1d-4b07-bcee-1f7f5e6cee2e","uuid":"3f4edb0c-e0fb-422d-8b6c-510bd0ada8d4","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:10:47.404Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3NKMcn7vEonuvgDySNT"}
